# SPA rewrites for the app's client routes ONLY (see src/app.tsx). Everything
# else that misses a static file serves public/404.html with a real 404.
#
# Deliberate and load-bearing: a catch-all /* rewrite used to answer missing
# /assets/* chunk URLs with index.html as HTTP 200. During a deploy's edge
# window that let browsers AND the service worker's install precache store
# HTML bodies under hashed .js/.css URLs, poisoning clients so the app could
# never boot (2026-08-05 incident). A 404 can never be cached as a module and
# a failed service worker install cleanly retries.
#
# Targets are /app (the pretty URL of app.html, a build-time copy of the
# shell) because Cloudflare Pages normalizes rewrites targeting /index.html
# into 308 redirects to /, which drops the requested path (it broke /about
# and Stripe's return to /unlocked when this was first attempted).
/project/*    /app    200
/unlocked     /app    200
/unlocked/*   /app    200
/about        /app    200
/privacy      /app    200
/terms        /app    200
/receive      /app    200
/receive/*    /app    200
